course: dictionary
lesson: 783
title: Becoming something new
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word become means to start to be something, or to change into something new over time. The context shows you which meaning fits. «The foxes became friendly and wagged their tails.» The foxes were not friendly at the start. Over time they changed, so became means changed into.
explain: Become is often followed by a new thing: «become friends», «become tired», «become a doctor». Ask yourself: what was it before, and what is it now? If the answer shows a change, become is probably the right word.
explain: Become does not always mean a big change. «Water becomes ice when it freezes.» The water has changed into a new form, and the sentence tells you what it changed into.
fact: Become means to start to be something, or to change into something new over time.
fact: A good check is to swap in turned into and see if the sentence still makes sense.
fact: «A seed becomes a plant.» «Tadpoles become frogs.»
fact: The past tense of become is became: «The beaver became a symbol of Canada.»
fact: Old-fashioned: «That dress becomes you» means it looks nice on you.
exercise: «The tadpoles became frogs over the summer.» What does became mean here? | *Changed into frogs | Sat on the bank | Swam very fast | Were sold at the shop
exercise: «The foxes became friendly and wagged their tails.» Find and copy the word that shows the change. | tails | foxes | *became | wagged
exercise: «That red hat becomes you.» What does becomes you suggest? | It belongs to someone else | *It looks nice on you | It is made of red wool | It is too big for you
test: «Water becomes ice when it freezes.» What happens to the water? | It falls as rain | *It turns into ice | It boils away into steam | It gets heavier
test: «The beaver became a symbol of Canada.» What is the best meaning of became? | *Turned into | Ran away from | Was hidden from | Stopped being
exam: «A caterpillar becomes a butterfly.» Which sentence has the same meaning? | The caterpillar sat on a leaf and slept | The butterfly flew over the garden | Caterpillars eat leaves and grow | *The caterpillar turned into a butterfly
